      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 1328: 🔴 `maybeReopenVideoCodec` frees the active video encoder (`avcodec_free_context`) before confirming that `initVideoStream(framesCtx)` succeeds. If reopen fails (e.g., transient HW init/open failure), the session is left without a usable encoder and subsequent `encode()` calls return errors, effectively dropping video permanently. Build the replacement encoder first (or keep a backup pointer), and only swap/free the old context after successful initialization; otherwise restore the previous context and keep `pendingCodecReopen_` set for retry.",
      "revId": "7bff9db28cd403d9d510a9cde391b7d201cdd093",
